claim.claim-text:
receiving, by control logic, data pertaining to selection of a first training program;
transmitting, by the control logic, media instructions to cause activation of the media player, wherein the media player is configured to display visual data corresponding to the first training program;
transmitting, by the control logic, ball-throwing instructions to cause activation of the ball-throwing machine configured to impart motion to one or more balls in accordance with the first training program;
obtaining, by the control logic, image data of an interaction between a first player and a first ball of the one or more balls, wherein the interaction includes at least receipt of the first ball by the first player or a striking of the first ball by the first player; and
responsive to receiving the image data, performing, by the control logic, operations of generating and transmitting second media instructions to cause updating of the visual data by the media play, wherein the updating includes display of an indication of an accuracy of the interaction relative to instructions of the first training program.

a ball-throwing machine configured to impart motion to one or more balls;
a media player; and
one or more logic modules stored on a non-transitory storage medium, the one or more logic modules including instructions, upon execution by one or more processors, perform operations including:

receiving data pertaining to selection of a first training program;
transmitting media instructions to cause activation of the media player, wherein the media player is configured to display visual data corresponding to the first training program;
transmitting ball-throwing instructions to cause activation of the ball-throwing machine configured to impart motion to one or more balls in accordance with the first training program;
obtaining image data of an interaction between a first player and a first ball of the one or more balls, wherein the interaction includes at least receipt of the first ball by the first player or a striking of the first ball by the first player; and
responsive to receiving the image data, performing operations of generating and transmitting second media instructions to cause updating of the visual data by the media play, wherein the updating includes display of an indication of an accuracy of the interaction relative to instructions of the first training program.
